cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying ICML 2026 paper."
title: "Effective Model Pruning: Measuring the Redundancy of Model Components"
abstract: >
  Effective Model Pruning (EMP) supplies a universal adaptive threshold for neural
  network pruning, derived from the effective sample size of the importance score
  distribution (the inverse Simpson index). A tight lower bound on the preserved
  mass and an upper bound on the loss change under magnitude pruning are proven,
  and the method is validated on FC, CNN, ResNet, Kolmogorov Arnold, GPT 2, and
  LLaMA family models, as well as on image features.
